==English==

===Etymology===
{{compound|goof|ball|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈɡufˌbɔl/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-goofball.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|informal|derogatory|lang=en}} A [[foolish]] or [[silly]] person.
#: ''If that '''goofball''' would put half the effort into her studies as she does into her juggling, she might do very well.''
# {{context|informal|lang=en}} A [[pill]] or [[tablet]] containing a [[pharmaceutical]] which has [[hypnotic]] or [[intoxicate|intoxicating]] effects, especially a [[barbiturate]].
#* '''1953''' April 27, "[http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,818313,00.html Capsules]," ''Time'':
#*: Strong Cobb & Co. of Cleveland announced a new barbiturate which in overlarge doses will turn the stomachs of "'''goofball'''" addicts and would-be suicides.
